  "notes": "Image: 'Pimoroni Tiny 2040 - Pins and Dims'. Peripheral functions combine the column header (SPI/I2C/UART) with the printed peripheral number, per the image KEY ('0 SDA' under I2C = I2C0 SDA). 'CONSOLE' spans the GP0/GP1 UART0 entries. Silkscreen spellings are listed first in functions (5V, 3V, A0-A3, 0-7). The D-shaped silkscreen glyphs beside pins 2 and 8 (GND) are treated as symbols and omitted. Skipped: the back-view RESET/BOOT buttons and RGB LED callout (RUN, GP18-GP20, GP23 are on-board signals, not wiring points), and the USB-C connector."
